    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Build a Bike Safety Bot\r\n\r\nThe City Bike Program Coordinator set up this bot to help those who are trying to better understand how to recycle — but they weren't careful about what information they gave it.\r\n\r\nThis is supposed to help with topics like helmets, where to ride, signaling, riding at night, and checking your bike.\r\n\r\n##### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Start by asking your bot one big question — something like what a person new to this would want to know overall. Then ask a few follow-ups. Notice where it can't give you a straight answer.\r\n2. Open the Retrieval panel. That's everything your bot knows. Read through it.\r\n3. Fix the retrieval information. You can delete cards or edit them to fix them. Some cards are a judgement call - decide what you would trust.\r\n4. Click Update, then ask your questions again. Keep going until you would trust this bot with a first-time rider.\r\n5. Try asking something your bot has no information about. What does it say now?\r\n\r\n##### Talk with your partner:\r\nCompare bots — did you keep or edit the same things? Does having retrieval information mean the bot is always right?\r\n\r\n::: details [**Have Time To Make It Better?**]\r\nAdd any of these to your bot's retrieval information, then test whether it helps:\r\n\r\n- [Updated April 2026] Look and listen before entering an intersection, even when you\r\nhave the right of way. Slow down and be ready to stop.\r\n- [Updated April 2026] Keep both hands on the handlebars except when signaling. Do not\r\nride while holding a phone.\r\n- [Updated April 2026] Wear bright or light-colored clothing during the day and something\r\nreflective at night so drivers can see you sooner.\r\n\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [**Ready for a challenge?**]\r\nFind one more fact this bot should know. Write it as a new retrieval entry — include the date and where you found it, just like the other cards do. Then test whether your bot uses it.\r\n:::\r\n",
    "aichat_settings": {
      "initialCustomizations": {
        "selectedModelId": "gemini-2.5-flash",
        "temperature": 0.5,
        "systemPrompt": "You are a bike safety assistant for the city's new bike share program. A city bike program coordinator built you to help new riders learn how to ride safely.",
        "retrievalContexts": [
          "[Updated April 2026] Always wear a helmet, every ride, no matter how short the trip.\nThe helmet should sit level on your head and fit snugly.",
          "[Updated April 2026] Use hand signals before turning or stopping so drivers and other\nriders know what you are about to do.",
          "[Updated 2016] At night, use a white light on the front of your bike and a red light\nor reflector on the back so you are visible. Hand signals are not necessary as long\nas you make eye contact with drivers.",
          "[Updated April 2026] Bike share memberships can be purchased monthly or annually, and\nthe first 30 minutes of each ride is included at no extra charge.",
          "Check your tires, brakes, and chain before riding. A quick check takes less than a\nminute and catches most problems.",
          "[Updated April 2026] Riders should be aware of their surroundings and ride\nresponsibly at all times.",
          "[Updated 2013] Ride facing oncoming traffic so that you can see cars coming toward\nyou and react in time.",
          "[Updated April 2026] Ride in the same direction as traffic, on the right side of the\nroad, so drivers see you where they expect to see you."
        ],
